[[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The CODE control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20 is supplied\nwith power at pin 3 from the battery from the line of maxifuse EFI\nB99, through a  line protected by fuse F5 of the additional fuse\nbox B98 A.</strong></p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (15/54)\narrives at pin 8 from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the\nadditional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 4 is earthed.</p><p>The line leading from pin 6 is a serial\nline leading to engine management unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which is responsible\nfor identifying the key and exchanging codes.</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nunit that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthis receives signals from pin 5 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through\nthe tester line.</p><p>The self-test system also produces the signal\nfor the &#x27;CODE failure&#x27; warning light, located in the check instrument \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which comes out of pin 2 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The check module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30 receives a supply\ncontrolled by the ignition (INT) at pin 13 from the line protected\nby fuse F4 of supplementary fuse box B98B; when this earth signal\narrives, the &#x27;CODE failure&#x27; warning light comes on.</strong></p><p>A second control unit connector is connected\nvia two leads to the aerial, fitted coaxially to the ignition key,\nin order to detect key insertion and rotation.</p>"]]